\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Prospective 3D Controlled Ablation Benchmark across Three Operational Wind Farms. (a) High sensitivity to prior misspecification under strong constraints on Penmanshiel ($N_{\text  {train}}=1,583$): authentic physical guidance provides downside risk protection ($-1.22\%$), whereas disrupting the physical mapping (Pseudo-Scrambled prior) triggers a $+68.1\%$ surge in operational dispatch cost. (b) Low-$\lambda $ numerical regularization mimicry on Kelmarsh ($N=5,098$), where genuine and scrambled priors yield near-identical decision costs at $\lambda = 0.01$, indicating non-specific numerical regularization rather than physical domain reasoning. (c) Monotonic cost inflation under training proxy staleness: dispatch cost escalation across all three farms as historical wind proxy lag $k$ in the training loss increases from 1h to 6h. (d) Decoupling of symmetric point error (RMSE) from asymmetric decision risk ($r=2$), demonstrating that point metrics mask tail operational hazards.}}{13}{figure.caption.17}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:causal_ablation}{{4}{13}{Prospective 3D Controlled Ablation Benchmark across Three Operational Wind Farms. (a) High sensitivity to prior misspecification under strong constraints on Penmanshiel ($N_{\text {train}}=1,583$): authentic physical guidance provides downside risk protection ($-1.22\%$), whereas disrupting the physical mapping (Pseudo-Scrambled prior) triggers a $+68.1\%$ surge in operational dispatch cost. (b) Low-$\lambda $ numerical regularization mimicry on Kelmarsh ($N=5,098$), where genuine and scrambled priors yield near-identical decision costs at $\lambda = 0.01$, indicating non-specific numerical regularization rather than physical domain reasoning. (c) Monotonic cost inflation under training proxy staleness: dispatch cost escalation across all three farms as historical wind proxy lag $k$ in the training loss increases from 1h to 6h. (d) Decoupling of symmetric point error (RMSE) from asymmetric decision risk ($r=2$), demonstrating that point metrics mask tail operational hazards}{figure.caption.17}{}}
