\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Within-Site Learning Curves across Sample Sizes $N_{\text  {train}} \in \{500, 1000, 1500, 3000, 5000\}$ on Kelmarsh and Hill of Towie (Multi-seed means and standard deviations). Decoupling sample volume from topography confirms that fixed historical physical priors provide lower dispatch costs across both sites under restricted model training windows ($N_{\text  {train}} \le 1,000$, $-2.00\%$ on Kelmarsh and $-3.62\%$ on Hill of Towie), whereas expanding model training windows to $N_{\text  {train}} = 5,000$ closes this gap and slightly reverses the ranking (+0.33\% on Kelmarsh, +1.73\% on Hill of Towie). In contrast, misspecified scrambled priors under strong regularization ($\lambda =1.0$) induce severe dispatch cost penalties ($+43\%$ to $+98\%$) across all sample regimes.}}{14}{figure.caption.18}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:within_site_learning_curve}{{5}{14}{Within-Site Learning Curves across Sample Sizes $N_{\text {train}} \in \{500, 1000, 1500, 3000, 5000\}$ on Kelmarsh and Hill of Towie (Multi-seed means and standard deviations). Decoupling sample volume from topography confirms that fixed historical physical priors provide lower dispatch costs across both sites under restricted model training windows ($N_{\text {train}} \le 1,000$, $-2.00\%$ on Kelmarsh and $-3.62\%$ on Hill of Towie), whereas expanding model training windows to $N_{\text {train}} = 5,000$ closes this gap and slightly reverses the ranking (+0.33\% on Kelmarsh, +1.73\% on Hill of Towie). In contrast, misspecified scrambled priors under strong regularization ($\lambda =1.0$) induce severe dispatch cost penalties ($+43\%$ to $+98\%$) across all sample regimes}{figure.caption.18}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Continuous Prior Corruption and Engineering Drift Severity Response Curves. (a) Continuous interpolation between authentic and scrambled priors $\alpha \in [0.0, 1.0]$, identifying an empirical crossover region around $\alpha \approx 0.07$ on Penmanshiel before physical regularizers worsen unconstrained dispatch costs. (b) Turbine aerodynamic aging: capacity derating exceeding 10\% flips nominal physical priors into economic penalties. (c) Anemometer sensor calibration drift: Penmanshiel retains an advantage under positive wind speed drift up to $+15\%$, whereas negative sensor under-reporting systematically inflates shortfall.}}{14}{figure.caption.19}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:corruption_gradient}{{6}{14}{Continuous Prior Corruption and Engineering Drift Severity Response Curves. (a) Continuous interpolation between authentic and scrambled priors $\alpha \in [0.0, 1.0]$, identifying an empirical crossover region around $\alpha \approx 0.07$ on Penmanshiel before physical regularizers worsen unconstrained dispatch costs. (b) Turbine aerodynamic aging: capacity derating exceeding 10\% flips nominal physical priors into economic penalties. (c) Anemometer sensor calibration drift: Penmanshiel retains an advantage under positive wind speed drift up to $+15\%$, whereas negative sensor under-reporting systematically inflates shortfall}{figure.caption.19}{}}
